The intake service keeps no secrets of its own. On the VM the unit reads two
files that other services already own:

  /opt/chat-service/.env     SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   (the Hub)
  /opt/whatsapp-filer/.env   AZURE_TENANT_ID, AZURE_CLIENT_ID, AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET,
                             SHAREPOINT_SITE, DATA_ROOM_PATH            (SharePoint, app-only)

Both are listed as EnvironmentFile= in deploy/intake@.service, so nothing is
copied. If either file moves, change those two lines and `systemctl daemon-reload`.

On a Mac the same names are read from intake-service/.env, the repo's .env, and
~/AKLA - Agenda Extractor/.env (see intake/config.py), or from INTAKE_ENV, a
colon-separated list of .env paths that replaces that list.
